 in the  80s and 90s and and that we're facing  all over again right at this time and  it's a real tribute to to Steve's book  that it received a wonderful review by  somebody who I dare say is a lot more  conservative then Steve is yesterday in  the New York Times a great of  a review by Bob Samuelson which pointed  out what a fair-minded and and and fun  to read book it is which it is so um  thank you very much Steve iners  congratulations to you and the books are  for sale in the front of the store  you're watching book TV 48 hours of  nonfiction books coming up at midnight  Eastern a look at the influence of  Wahhabi Islam and its ties to the Saudi  royal family with Stephen Schwartz  author of the two faces of Islam then  meditations of Marcus Aurelius with  translator Gregory Hays Sunday night  Robert remedy profiles Mormon Church  founder Joseph Smith after that on  public lives a panel featuring  biographers Robert Kira
 

